Hello, guys and gals, and welcome back to another FNF_Thoughts blog post, coming at ya from somewhere on Earth
I promised y’all to share my opinions about the Mobile port of Friday Night Funkin and that’s exactly what I’m gonna do
Now, to clarify, the reason I’m calling FNF:Mobile as a port rather than a separate game is because one, FNF is primarily a PC game and two, 
because of the opinions I have on it
So, without further ado, let’s talk about it

Alright, there are many aspects I want to cover but let’s start with the gameplay mechanics
As most of you who have played the game by now know, there is no upscroll setting just yet, but I think I prefer playing downscroll
(this coming from a player who uses upscroll on the desktop version)
I also kinda like being able to use two hands to play a song (coming from a guy who loves using one hand to press the keys)
The only complaint I have is that I have literally no idea where the hitboxes are for each of the notes
I have to basically guess and hope that I’m as to the specific field where my thumbs should go
I think I need to install a hitbox mod from GameBanana or something of that sort in order to get the best experience possible

Alright, now let’s talk about the actual game itself
It’s about as much fun as playing on Desktop is (unless you’re really into tapping screens) and it runs pretty smoothly
I will say though, not being able to finish Weekend 1 kinda takes from the overall experience
I heard they fixed it with a patch in 0.7.2 or 0.7.3 so maybe I’ll head back to the mobile port later
One huge complaint I have is that, even on Low power Mode, the app drains my phone battery. 
To put it in perspective, after playing for about one hour, about 16% was drained
I guess that’s to be expected though from a game with so many assets and moving parts

Anyways, that’s all I have to say about the Mobile port
What, you thought this was gonna be a long one, right, but unfortunately, there’s only so many opinions I have over it
It’s basically just FNF but downscroll always enabled and hitboxes are tiny for tapping

Thanks for reading, maybe consider giving me a follow or perhaps starring this repo if you want more fire content
Have an amazing rest of the day/night and stay knightly, my friends
Goooodbyeee
